OL,3,GNEWSADeputy head hopes poker will boost
OL,4,Apension
OL,5,
OL,6,FA deputy headteacher who took up poker
OL,7,Fas she approached her 50th birthday
OL,8,Fsaid she hoped to top up her pension by
OL,9,Fplaying in tournaments around the world
OL,10,Fwhen she eventually retires.
OL,12,FNicki Kelsall, from Nuneaton, only
OL,13,Fstarted playing the card game about
OL,14,Fthree years ago, after being invited to
OL,15,Fattend a beginners' poker night run by
OL,16,Fher brother.
OL,18,FDespite being a bit nervous having
OL,19,Fnever played it before, she said she
OL,20,F"loved every minute" and went on to win
OL,21,Fher first tournament.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,354,350,200,160,0,100
